The C++ stack is an incremental migration of the ARIEC61850 C# implementation. The C# source
remains the behavioral oracle until deterministic cross-language comparison and isolated
physical-laboratory interoperability are accepted.

Phase 4C/4C.1 includes an explicitly invoked TCP transport, a read-only MMS discovery surface,
a C#-compatible `live-ied-model-v1` mapper, parity tooling, and physical evidence runners. The
discovery surface does not construct MMS Write, control, GI, RCB reservation/enable, dynamic
DataSet mutation, or file-service requests.

Physical IED compatibility is target-specific and must not be inferred from synthetic,
loopback, or simulated evidence. Review `PHASE_4C1_LIVE_MODEL_INTEROP.md` and the lab checklist
before accepting a target.
